[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Strings: String Manipulation (Concatenation, Substrings, Reversal)"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Strings are fundamental data structures used to represent sequences of characters. Manipulating strings is a common task in many programming applications. This tutorial covers essential string manipulation techniques: concatenation, extracting substrings, and reversing strings."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"String Concatenation"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Concatenation is the process of joining two or more strings together to create a new, combined string. Most programming languages provide operators or functions to perform string concatenation."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"// Example (Python)
string1 = "Hello"
string2 = "World"
result = string1 + " " + string2  # Concatenation using the '+' operator
print(result) # Output: Hello World"},{"order":6,"type":"code","text":"// Example (Java)
String string1 = "Hello";
String string2 = "World";
String result = string1 + " " + string2; // Concatenation using the '+' operator
System.out.println(result); // Output: Hello World"},{"order":7,"type":"code","text":"// Example (JavaScript)
let string1 = "Hello";
let string2 = "World";
let result = string1 + " " + string2; // Concatenation using the '+' operator
console.log(result); // Output: Hello World"},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"Extracting Substrings"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"A substring is a contiguous sequence of characters within a string. Extracting substrings involves retrieving a portion of a string based on specified start and end indices."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"// Example (Python)
string = "This is a string"
substring = string[0:4]  # Extract characters from index 0 up to (but not including) index 4
print(substring) # Output: This"},{"order":11,"type":"code","text":"// Example (Java)
String string = "This is a string";
String substring = string.substring(0, 4); // Extract characters from index 0 up to (but not including) index 4
System.out.println(substring); // Output: This"},{"order":12,"type":"code","text":"// Example (JavaScript)
let string = "This is a string";
let substring = string.substring(0, 4); // Extract characters from index 0 up to (but not including) index 4
console.log(substring); // Output: This"},{"order":13,"type":"subheading","text":"String Reversal"},{"order":14,"type":"paragraph","text":"Reversing a string means rearranging its characters in reverse order. This can be achieved using various techniques, including iteration, recursion, or built-in functions."},{"order":15,"type":"code","text":"// Example (Python)
string = "hello"
reversed_string = string[::-1] # Using slicing to reverse the string
print(reversed_string) # Output: olleh"},{"order":16,"type":"code","text":"// Example (Java)
String string = "hello";
String reversedString = new StringBuilder(string).reverse().toString();
System.out.println(reversedString); // Output: olleh"},{"order":17,"type":"code","text":"// Example (JavaScript)
let string = "hello";
let reversedString = string.split('').reverse().join('');
console.log(reversedString); // Output: olleh"},{"order":18,"type":"paragraph","text":"These string manipulation techniques are essential for various tasks, including data processing, text analysis, and algorithm development. Understanding and applying these techniques effectively will improve your ability to work with string data."}]
